==English==

===Noun===
{{en-noun|sg= a [[blue]] [[moon]]}}

# {{rare}} The [[moon]] [[tinted]] towards [[blue]] as it appears in the sky, caused by dust or smoke in the atmosphere.
# {{archaic}} Something [[absurd]].
#* '''1528''', ''Rede Me and Be Not Wrothe'', pamphlet
#*: Yf they say the '''mone''' is '''belewe''', we must believe that it is true.
# {{obsolete}} The third [[full moon]] in a [[quarter]] that contains four rather than the usual three full moons.
# {{idiom}} {{context|by extension}} A long time.

===Etymology===
Mistake in Sky & Telescope magazine in 1946 led to the use of a incorrect definition of the expression (see below). The definition was retracted nearly 60 years later.

===Noun===
{{wikipedia}}
''a'' '''blue moon'''

# The [[second]] of two [[full moon]]s that occur in the same calendar [[month]]. (Note: This is the mistaken definition of the expression that is referred to in the section "Etymology". Sky & Telescope provides an article explaining the definition and how the mistake was introduced. [http://www.skyandtelescope.com/observing/objects/moon/3304131.html?page=1&c=y].)

